2026-11-15T17:27:11.3204483Z {"type": "result", "result": "I have not produced a model. I reached the end of a working budget while still inside drawing interpretation, and writing a route now would mean guessing the numbers the gates are measured against \u2014 which the task explicitly says is worse than delivering nothing.\n\n## What is actually in the workspace\n\n`/app/files/dc_model__hall_seed000_d000__mep_routing/output/solution.py` is still the original raising stub. It does not build an IFC file, so `tools/clash_check.py` cannot be run on anything I produced: there is no `model.ifc`, no `HARD CLASHES` count, no connectivity chain, no coverage fraction.\n\n## What I did establish, and can defend\n\n- No image library is needed and I did not need one: all seven PNGs decode with `zlib` + `numpy` alone into `work/*.npy` (RGBA, `1100\u00d71600\u00d74`). `work/A101rgb.npy` is the decoded A-101 in RGB.\n- **All seven sheets share one drawing viewport**: ink bounding box `x150\u20131377, y78\u20131019`. Left border triple-rule at x147\u2013152, right border at x1355, top frame y77, bottom frame y1022\u20131027. Those are read from the decoded pixels, not assumed.\n- **The column grid is the reliable geometry on A-101**: plan grid verticals at x 350, 369, 463, 523, 586, 660, 730, 818, 866, 978, 1074, 1355; left wall inner face x152, right wall x1355. Long horizontal rules at y194/241\u2013243/258/280\u2013281/297\u2013298/312\u2013314/329/417\u2013419/449/592/781\u2013782/994. The plan therefore occupies roughly 1203 px across; no dimension string on any sheet decodes, so **the px\u2192mm scale is still unfixed** \u2014 that is the single biggest blocker and it is why I have no row spans to report.\n- **A-601/A-602 schedule structure**: a real ruled table, not text blocks. A-601 has a full-width dark data band at y304\u2013306, cell rules at x600/740/818 and y417\u2013419/449; A-602's cells run x460\u2013790 with identical y rules. Cell contents are glyphs I could see but not transcribe reliably.\n- **M-101 and E-101 service-entry symbol located**: the entry occurs at the *same* pixel block on both sheets, a framed symbol at roughly `x1083\u20131115, y181\u2013227` (E-101 also shows busway blocks at `x1146\u20131177`). That is the best evidence for the entry I have, but I have not completed the cross-check against the border dimensions and the A-101 plan, so per the instruction I am recording it as **ENTRY_UNKNOWN** rather than inventing a coordinate.\n\n## What is unfinished\n\n1. px\u2192mm scale calibration (no dimension string decoded; A-301 section lines not tied to a stated level).\n2. Rack row count and cabinets-per-row straight off A-601/A-602 \u2014 without this, any coverage figure would be measured over rows I invented.\n3. CRAH/PDU footprints from M-101/E-101 colour masks (located in pixel terms, not yet converted).\n4. A-301 elevations for the three services, and hence the 2600 mm headroom and 460 mm sprinkler-deflector checks.\n\nEverything downstream \u2014 routing, connectivity chain, clash count \u2014 depends on 1\u20134, so every gate would currently be a guess. The correct call is `ENTRY_UNKNOWN` and stop, which is where the deliverable stands.\n\nIf you want me to continue, the highest-value next step is decoding the A-301 section datum and the A-601 cabinet-dimension cells (both are ruled tables with recoverable glyphs), because those two readings fix the scale and the row schedule, and everything else follows from them."}
